-- title:
--   Residue-preserving swaps of multicores imply Jantzen equivalence
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field, let $n,r\ge1$, let $q\in F^\times$ with $q\ne1$, and fix integer charges $c_1,\ldots,c_r$, with $Q_a=q^{c_a}$. Let $e$ be the least $k\ge2$ with $1+q+\cdots+q^{k-1}=0$, or $\infty$ if there is none. For an $r$-multipartition $\lambda$ of $n$, each node $(i,j,a)$ has charged residue $j-i+c_a$ modulo $e$, interpreted as an integer when $e=\infty$. Residue multiplicities count nodes individually. The relation $\sim_J$ is the equivalence relation generated by nonzero coefficients $J_{\alpha\beta}$ in Definition 2.5, with intermediate multipartitions of the same size.
--
--   Let $\overline\lambda,\overline\mu$ be the componentwise $e$-cores of two multipartitions $\lambda,\mu$ of $n$. For component indices $a,b$ and runners $i,j$, let $s_{ij}^{ab}$ be the legal packed-abacus swap of Definition 3.10(a): transfer one bead from runner $i$ to runner $j$ in component $a$ and one in the reverse direction in component $b$, keeping the other components fixed. When $e=\infty$, each runner is an integer position, and the source's bead/gap occupancy conditions are required. Then
--
--   $$
--   \lambda\sim_C\mu\quad\text{and}\quad
--   \overline\mu=s_{ij}^{ab}(\overline\lambda)
--   \quad\Longrightarrow\quad
--   \lambda\sim_J\mu.
--   $$
--
--   The relation $\sim_C$ means equality of the charged residue multiplicities. This statement applies the swap to the cores, while allowing the original multipartitions to contain removable hooks.
--
--   **Formalization Note** A legal relation is used instead of a total swap function. Both opposite transfers must exist and give packed abacuses. Illegal or inconsistent swaps have no assigned output.
-- source:
--   Blocks of cyclotomic Hecke algebras, arXiv:math/0607451v4, PDF p. 15, Lemma 3.11

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Intake100_P29

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Intake100.P29

noncomputable section

open scoped BigOperators Classical

variable {F : Type} [Field F]

/-- Lemma 3.11, PDF p. 15: both operands of the swap are multicores;
the residue hypothesis concerns the original shapes. -/
theorem core_swap_jantzen {r n : ℕ} (hr : 0 < r) (hn : 0 < n)
    (q : F) (hq : q ≠ 0) (hqOne : q ≠ 1) (c : Fin r → ℤ)
    (L M : Multipartition r) (hL : size L = n) (hM : size M = n)
    (a b : Fin r) (i j : ZMod (quantumCharacteristic q))
    (hres : ChargedResidueEquivalent (quantumCharacteristic q) c L M)
    (hswap : CoreSwap (quantumCharacteristic q) c
      (multicore (quantumCharacteristic q) L) (multicore (quantumCharacteristic q) M) a b i j) :
    JantzenEquivalent q (fun d => q ^ c d) L M := by sorry

end

end QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Intake100.P29
